{"availability":"available","full":"CodesWhat/drydock","name":"drydock","description":"Open source container update monitoring — 23 registries, 20 notification triggers, audit log, OIDC auth, Prometheus metrics, and a modern dashboard.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":261,"forks":14,"created":"2026-02-08T20:09:53Z","updated":"2026-10-08T19:54:34Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://getdrydock.com","topics":["containers","devops","docker","docker-compose","homelab","monitoring","notifications","prometheus","self-hosted","typescript","vuejs","watchtower-alternative"],"demo":"https://demo.getdrydock.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:46.702Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:46.702Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:46.702Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:57.771Z","stars":260,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:31.662Z","stars":260,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:39.754Z","stars":261,"forks":14},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:07:46.702Z","stars":261,"forks":14}],"technologies":["Vue"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["English · Español · Polski · 简体中文 · Deutsch · Français · Português (Brasil)","Container images drift out of date silently. A base image patches a CVE, an app cuts a release, a tag moves. Unless you're watching every registry by hand, your running containers fall behind until something breaks or gets exploited.","Most tools force a tradeoff. The auto-updaters (Watchtower, Ouroboros) pull and restart with little visibility or control, and are now largely unmaintained. The dashboards (Portainer) manage containers but aren't built for update intelligence. Drydock is monitor-first: it watches 23 registries and tells you exactly what changed (major, minor, patch, or digest) before anything happens, then acts only when you let it. And it goes further than any of them. Trivy/Grype vulnerability scanning blocks unsafe updates, cosign verifies signatures, pre-update image backups roll back automatically on…"],"features":["How does drydock compare to other container update tools?","✅ = supported ❌ = not supported ⚠️ = partial / limited ? = unconfirmed † = archived, no longer maintained","Watchtower was archived in December 2025 and its last release was v1.7.1 (November 2023). An unofficial community fork, nicholas-fedor/watchtower, is still actively released.","Compiled from each project's public documentation and repositories, 2026-08-29. Contributions welcome if any information is inaccurate."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CodesWhat/drydock/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3025ee7d4f8dd0aa94f3fde26bebbd39f74b078a378cd0988296f20efea5b49d","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T16:35:44.584Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:36:20.282Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"English · Español · Polski · 简体中文 · Deutsch · Français · Português (Brasil)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CodesWhat/drydock/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Most tools force a tradeoff. The auto-updaters (Watchtower, Ouroboros) pull and restart with little visibility or control, and are now largely unmaintained. The dashboards (Portainer) manage containers but aren't built for update intelligence. Drydock is monitor-first: it watches 23 registries and tells you exactly what changed (major, minor, patch, or digest) before anything…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CodesWhat/drydock/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3025ee7d4f8dd0aa94f3fde26bebbd39f74b078a378cd0988296f20efea5b49d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CodesWhat/drydock/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:36:20.283Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T19:54:34Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CodesWhat/drydock/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:36:20.285Z","hash":"3025ee7d4f8dd0aa94f3fde26bebbd39f74b078a378cd0988296f20efea5b49d","originalBytes":38661,"storedBytes":38661,"